# warrig media-automation stack (2026-08-24): torrents + arr-managed media
# under ~/data are bulk replaceable content, deliberately not backed up.
# rsnapshot passes --relative, so exclude anchoring is against / and paths
# arrive as /home/nux/data/... Patterns must carry the full path (same as
# the /home/nux/home/ entry above). Bare /data/... never matches. Only warrig
# has these; citadel has no ~/data.
/home/nux/data/torrents/
/home/nux/data/media/

# --- 2026-08-31 -------------------------------------------------------------
# Cache and Downloads. warrig's /home/nux is 1.9T; data/torrents (1.5T) was
# already excluded but .cache (249G) was not, so the hourly pull scanned ~400 GB
# and the 01:00 run did not finish until 02:25, overrunning its own slot.
# borgmatic already excludes both on warrig ("*/.cache/*", "*/Downloads/*"),
# so this only brings rsnapshot in line with the other tier.
**/.cache/
**/Downloads/

